<%# Allocation dialog (round 26 R4 re-org — owner items 6/7/8/9; supersedes
    the round 20 two-disclosure-stack layout). ALL three instances share
    this partial (allocation:new with the known list + CTA,
    allocation:selected, the per-allocation edit), so the layout is
    identical for new + edit: NO collapsibles. The form is a flat grid:
      Row 1: Name | Linked bill (the linked row is grey — text-secondary —
        when a bill is linked; the RT select for custom rows).
      Row 2: Amount (with the Mode sub-row) | Cadence.
      Row 3: Bank source — a labeled row on a darker background (item 6):
        the trigger shows ONLY the active selection (bank avatar + name +
        ****last4, or a profile icon + "None Selected"); clicking opens a
        floating dropdown panel (position:fixed z-50, placed under the
        trigger, viewport-clamped) holding the bank-row radio list. The
        radios live OUTSIDE the <form> (a same-name hidden input + radio
        in one form would serialize as an array) — the form's hidden
        plan_allocation[account_id] input is the submit carrier, synced by
        JS (#applyBankSelection). The panel stays a DOM descendant of the
        dialog's content target, so a click inside it never looks like a
        backdrop click (round 26 R3 clickOutside lesson).
      Row 4: Category — the floating DS::Popover trigger IS the labeled
        row (item 7b: the trigger carries the same colored icon chip the
        popup rows do); category auto-fill (item 7a): a linked bill's own
        category (recurring_transaction.category_id) is preselected when
        the allocation carries none.
    Linked (pre-determined bill) allocations render name / amount / cadence
    as READ-ONLY context (hidden inputs carry the values so the save
    contract is unchanged); the linked-context hint explains why (the hint
    + the locked-row pencil tooltips moved INSIDE the value boxes,
    hover-only — item 8).
    Kind is a HIDDEN input (item 7c: the visible kind select is gone; all
    JS consumers query by name). DYNAMIC BY TYPE: the form reshapes to the
    kind (mode / cadence / detected-bill link only for Bill / Debt; name +
    monthly amount for Savings / Fun Money) — the JS reshaping lives in
    plan_flow_controller.js (#applyAllocationVisibility / #setFieldLocked /
    #setAllocationMode), unchanged.
    The open paths (Known Allocations list, New Allocation, Recommended
    prefills) and the in-place submit are unchanged.
    Round 21 T3/T4: the CTA rides the dialog header (new allocation only)
    and the partial renders a SECOND time as the "selected allocation"
    window (node_id "allocation:selected", show_known: false) — the known
    list + CTA live ONLY in the allocation:new instance so the in-place
    known-list swap keeps a single [data-plan-flow-target='knownSection']
    holder.
    locals: (allocation, known_allocations = [], known_hidden = false, node_id: nil, show_known: true) %>
<% is_new = allocation.nil? %>
<%# Round 21 T3/T4: the dialog node id + the known-section visibility are
    OPTIONAL locals (read via local_assigns — ActionView does not apply the
    comment defaults, and the edit-dialog render passes only allocation:).
    Defaults: allocation:new for a blank form, the allocation's id otherwise;
    the known list + header CTA show only for the allocation:new instance
    (show_known: false for the selected-allocation window). %>
<% node_id = local_assigns[:node_id] || (is_new ? "allocation:new" : "allocation:#{allocation.id}") %>
<% show_known = local_assigns.fetch(:show_known, true) %>
<%# kind: the allocation's kind, or the form default ("bill") for a new row.
    linked: the allocation is a pre-determined bill (a real detected bill
    record behind it) -> name / amount / cadence are read-only context,
    Mode does not appear, and the type options are Bill / Debt only. %>
<%# Round 26 R4 (item 7c): the kind is a HIDDEN input (the visible kind
    select is gone — all JS consumers query [name="plan_allocation[kind]"]
    by name; syncAllocationKind is now dead but harmless). The local is the
    hidden input's value. %>
<% kind = allocation&.kind.presence || "bill" %>
<% linked = allocation&.recurring_transaction_id.present? %>
<% linked_monthly = linked ? allocation.resolved_monthly_amount : nil %>
<%# The initial hidden class for the bill-only groups, mirroring what the
    JS (#applyAllocationVisibility) computes from the kind on change. %>
<% bucket_kind = %w[savings fun_money].include?(kind) %>
<%# Round 31A (Fun Money v2): the fun_money kind's config locals. The
    Ownership / Distribution / Mode / Matching fields render ONLY in the
    kind == "fun_money" branch (kind-conditional blocks — every other kind's
    dialog stays byte-identical, stop-rule). C11 defaults: a fresh row reads
    Household (legacy-safe — per-user matching is opt-in); Matching defaults
    to Equalize for member ownership (C11b). C12: the Name field is replaced
    by the Ownership select, but plan_allocation[name] still submits the
    constant kind label so the dialog title, the over-plan item label, and
    the graph allocations[].name stay stable. %>
<% fm_kind = kind == "fun_money" %>
<% fm_ownership = allocation&.ownership.presence || "household" %>
<% fm_distribution = allocation&.distribution.presence %>
<% fm_matching = allocation&.matching.presence || "equalize" %>
<% fm_raw_params = allocation&.distribution_params %>
<% fm_percents = fm_raw_params.is_a?(Hash) ?
                   ((fm_raw_params["percents"] || fm_raw_params[:percents] || {}).to_h) : {} %>
<%# Same member order as the planner's partners kwarg (created_at, id). %>
<% fm_members = @family_users || Current.family.users.order(:created_at, :id).to_a %>
<%# C15: several Fun Money rows — the FIRST one (sort order) drives the
    reconciliation; the dialog documents that here. %>
<% fm_rows_count = fm_kind ? Current.family.plan_allocations.where(kind: "fun_money").count : 0 %>
<%# Round 10 issue 4 / round 20 U: savings + fun_money labels for the
    account hint and the amount label (the bill label is the default). %>
<% account_hint = kind == "savings" ? t(".savings_account_hint") : (kind == "fun_money" ? t(".fun_account_hint") : t(".source_bank_hint")) %>
<% amount_label = kind == "savings" ? t(".savings_value_label") : (kind == "fun_money" ? t(".fun_value_label") : t(".value_label")) %>
<% amount_hint = kind == "savings" ? t(".savings_value_hint") : (kind == "fun_money" ? t(".fun_value_hint") : t(".required_hint")) %>
<%# Round 26 R4 (item 7a): the categories ONCE for the picker loop and the
    trigger's current-selection text + chip (server-side: No category / the
    category's display_name). Category auto-fill: a linked bill's own
    category is preselected when the allocation carries none (recurring
    transactions have carried category_id since the detected-bill work —
    belongs_to :category, optional). %>
<% categories_list = Current.family.categories.alphabetically_by_hierarchy.to_a %>
<% category_id = allocation&.category_id.presence || (linked ? allocation.recurring_transaction&.category_id : nil) %>
<% category_selection = category_id ? categories_list.find { |c| category_id.to_s == c.id.to_s } : nil %>
<% category_selection_text = category_selection ? category_selection.display_name : t(".category_none") %>
<% rt_recs = @graph[:recommendations].select { |rec| rec[:type] == "recurring_transaction" } %>
<%# The on-plan accounts the Bank source stack lists; plus the allocation's
    current account when it left the plan (so an edit cannot silently drop
    the link). %>
<% bank_rows = @in_plan_accounts.dup %>
<% unless is_new || allocation.account_id.blank? || @in_plan_account_ids.include?(allocation.account_id) %>
  <% off_plan = allocation.account %>
  <% bank_rows << off_plan if off_plan %>
<% end %>
<%# Round 21 T7: the header class override pins the header inside the
    dialog's OWN scroll container (the base classes below are duplicated
    verbatim from the DS::Dialog header slot — keep them in sync there).
    Scoped to the allocation dialogs only; every other dialog keeps the
    shared header behavior. %>
<%= render DS::Dialog.new(auto_open: false, disable_frame: true, width: "lg",
      data: { node_id: node_id }) do |dialog| %>
  <% dialog.with_header(class: "px-4 flex flex-col gap-2 sticky top-0 z-10 bg-container",
                        title: is_new ? t(".title_new") : t(".title_edit", name: allocation.name),
                        subtitle: t(".subtitle")) do %>
    <%# Round 21 T3: the CTA (new allocation only) moved from the footer row
        into the header, right-aligned. Round 25 R3: it now opens the
        4-kind picker (Bill / Debt / Savings / Fun Money) — picking a kind
        opens the blank form pre-set to it (the plan-flow#openAllocationKind
        action on the menu items; see _allocation_kind_picker.erb).
        wrapper_class self-end: the DS::Menu wrapper div is a block element
        in this flex-col header, so the sizing div keeps the menu trigger
        right-aligned at its own width (the button's self-end would be inert
        inside the block wrapper). %>
    <% if is_new && show_known %>
      <%= render "plan_flows/allocation_kind_picker",
            trigger_class: "shrink-0 text-sm bg-primary text-on-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 hover:opacity-90",
            label: t(".new_cta"),
            wrapper_class: "self-end" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% dialog.with_body do %>
    <%# In-place validation errors (owner round 3, R1/R7): the 422 response
        renders them here — no full-reload flash for in-place submits. %>
    <div data-in-place-errors class="hidden space-y-1"></div>
    <% if is_new && show_known %>
      <%# Known Allocations (F3; round 8): Sure's detected bills /
          subscriptions not already in the diagram — rows open the selected
          allocation window (round 21 T4). The partial is also re-rendered
          by the in-place JSON chrome so the list tracks allocation changes
          without a reload. Round 21 T3: the list sits in a darker, shorter
          sub-section; the footer CTA row is gone (button in the header). %>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-inset p-3 space-y-2">
        <%= render "plan_flows/known_allocations",
              known_allocations: known_allocations, known_hidden: known_hidden %>
        <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".new_hint") %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# In-place submit (owner round 3, R1/R7): data-turbo off + the
        in-place submit handler — the diagram tweens to the new graph
        instead of a full reload destroying it. family_currency feeds the
        JS currency formatting of the read-only amount rows. %>
    <%= form_with url: is_new ? flow_allocation_create_plan_path : flow_allocation_update_plan_path(allocation.id),
                  method: is_new ? :post : :patch,
                  scope: :plan_allocation,
                  class: "space-y-5" + (is_new && show_known ? " hidden" : ""),
                  data: { plan_flow_target: "allocationForm", turbo: "false", plan_flow_inplace: "true",
                          family_currency: Current.family.currency,
                          # Round 31A (C12): the constant Name for a
                          # fun_money row created via the kind picker (the
                          # blank form presets it client-side).
                          fun_money_default_name: t(".kind_fun_money") } do |form| %>
      <%# R35 (Flow Scenarios, design §4.4): scope the in-place write to the
          active scenario — the controller's load_scenario reads
          params[:scenario]. Absent on the Default (live) path. %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :scenario, @scenario.id if @scenario %>
      <%# Round 25 (Item 2): a target row (the bank dialog's "Make Allocated
          Sub-Account") keeps its dressed account through an allocation-
          dialog save — the hidden input carries the current target id; a
          plain row submits blank and stays plain (the sanitizer's
          .presence). The bank dialog's REVERSE (its kebab) is the only
          path that clears it. %>
      <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[target_account_id]"
             value="<%= allocation&.target_account_id %>">
      <%# Round 26 R4 (item 6): the bank-source hidden input — the submit
          carrier. The visible dropdown panel (rendered after the form,
          below) keeps the radio group plan_allocation[account_id] as the
          UI source of truth; JS syncs it here on every radio change
          (#applyBankSelection, plan_flow_controller.js). Two same-name
          controls in one form would serialize as an array and break
          sanitize_plan_allocation_row (find_by(id: array)). %>
      <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[account_id]"
             value="<%= allocation&.account_id %>">
      <%# Round 26 R4 (item 7c): the kind — a HIDDEN input on the current
          kind (the visible select is gone). Every JS consumer queries
          [name="plan_allocation[kind]"] by name; linked rows keep the
          server-fixed kind so there is no client leak. %>
      <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[kind]" value="<%= kind %>">
      <%# Round 26 R4 (item 7d): the layout — no collapsibles. The two
          disclosure stacks + the "More options" disclosure are dissolved:
          the linked-context hint (when linked), then Row 1 Name | Linked
          bill, Row 2 Amount (+ Mode sub-row) | Cadence, Row 3 Bank source
          (labeled row + floating dropdown), Row 4 Category (floating
          popover — the trigger IS the labeled row). The footer is
          unchanged. %>
      <% if linked %>
        <%# Disabled-state hint: explains why the bill details below are
            read-only (owner round 20: progressive disclosure). %>
        <p class="text-xs text-secondary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
          <%= t(".linked_context_hint") %>
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <%# Row 1: Name | Linked bill. %>
      <% if fm_kind %>
        <%# Row 1 (fun_money): Ownership | Distribution (C13 order 1+2). The
            Name field is replaced by the Ownership select (C12) — the
            hidden input keeps the save contract (the constant kind label;
            ownership is never written into name). The Distribution trigger
            opens the floating panel after the form (mirrors the bank
            Split Behavior + bank-source panel patterns: the radios carry
            their own names; the hidden plan_allocation[distribution] input
            is the submit carrier, synced by #syncFunDistribution). %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <label class="block text-xs text-secondary" for="fm_ownership_<%= node_id %>"><%= t(".ownership_label") %></label>
            <select id="fm_ownership_<%= node_id %>"
                    name="plan_allocation[ownership]"
                    class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full"
                    data-action="change->plan-flow#syncFunOwnership">
              <option value="household" <%= "selected" if fm_ownership == "household" %>><%= t(".ownership_household") %></option>
              <% fm_members.each do |member| %>
                <option value="<%= member.id %>" <%= "selected" if fm_ownership.to_s == member.id.to_s %>"><%= member.display_name %></option>
              <% end %>
            </select>
            <%# C12: the Name stays the constant kind label on save. %>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[name]" value="<%= t(".kind_fun_money") %>">
            <%# Submit carrier for the Distribution radio panel (which
                renders after the form — a same-name radio group in the
                form would serialize as an array). %>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[distribution]" value="<%= fm_distribution %>">
            <%# C9: the per-member percent carriers — one hidden input per
                family member, filled/cleared by JS as the panel's percent
                inputs change. Disabled + blank when the distribution is
                not "percent" (stale percents never submit; the sanitizer
                + model are the backstops). %>
            <% fm_members.each do |member| %>
              <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[distribution_percents][<%= member.id %>]"
                     value="<%= fm_distribution == "percent" ? fm_percents[member.id.to_s] : "" %>"
                     <%= "disabled" unless fm_distribution == "percent" %>>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-inset p-2">
            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->plan-flow#toggleFunDistribution"
                    data-fm-distribution-trigger
                    data-fm-distribution-none="<%= t('.distribution_none') %>"
                    class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-2 min-h-11 rounded-xl px-1 cursor-pointer">
              <span class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
                <span class="text-xs text-secondary shrink-0"><%= t(".distribution_label") %></span>
                <span class="text-sm <%= fm_distribution ? "text-primary" : "text-secondary" %> truncate" data-fm-distribution-label>
                  <%= fm_distribution ? t(".distribution_#{fm_distribution}") : t(".distribution_none") %>
                </span>
              </span>
              <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0" %>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% else %>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <%# Name: editable for a custom allocation; read-only context for
            a linked bill (the hidden input keeps the save contract).
            Round 26 R4 (item 8): the pencil tooltip sits INSIDE the value
            box (hover-only), not in the label row. %>
        <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-field="name">
          <% if linked %>
            <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".name_label") %></p>
            <div class="relative group">
              <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8 truncate"><%= allocation.name %></p>
              <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
              </span>
            </div>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[name]" value="<%= allocation.name %>">
          <% else %>
            <div data-allocation-field-state="editable">
              <%= form.label :name, t(".name_label"), class: "block text-xs text-secondary" %>
              <%= form.text_field :name,
                                 value: allocation&.name,
                                 required: true,
                                 class: "text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full" %>
            </div>
            <div data-allocation-field-state="locked" class="hidden">
              <div class="relative group">
                <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8 truncate" data-allocation-locked-value></p>
                <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                  <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
                </span>
              </div>
              <%# Carries the name on save while the editable control is
                  disabled (the disabled control would not submit). %>
              <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[name]" value="" disabled>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <% if linked %>
          <%# Row 1 right: the linked bill as read-only context — grey
              (text-secondary, round 26 R4 item 7d) so it reads as context,
              not an actionable control. The hidden input keeps the link on
              save. %>
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".linked_bill_label") %></p>
            <p class="text-sm text-secondary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 truncate">
              <%= allocation.recurring_transaction&.display_name || t(".rt_linked") %>
            </p>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[recurring_transaction_id]" value="<%= allocation.recurring_transaction_id %>">
          </div>
        <% else %>
          <%# Detected-bill link: the custom-allocation way to pull in a
              real bill (autofills name / amount / cadence / source bank
              and locks those fields read-only — the syncAllocationRt JS,
              unchanged). BILL-ONLY (data-allocation-kinds "bill"): the
              #applyAllocationVisibility kind loop hides it for debt,
              savings and fun money. %>
          <div class="space-y-1<%= bucket_kind ? " hidden" : "" %>" data-allocation-kinds="bill">
            <%= form.label :recurring_transaction_id, t(".link_rt_label"), class: "block text-xs text-secondary" %>
            <%= form.select :recurring_transaction_id,
                            options_for_select([[ t(".rt_none"), "" ]] + rt_recs.map { |rec| [ "#{rec[:name]} - #{number_to_currency(rec[:amount_cents] / 100.0, currency: Current.family.currency)}", rec[:recurring_transaction_id] ] } +
                                               (allocation&.recurring_transaction_id && !rt_recs.any? { |rec| rec[:recurring_transaction_id] == allocation.recurring_transaction_id } ? [[ t(".rt_linked"), allocation.recurring_transaction_id ]] : []),
                                               allocation&.recurring_transaction_id),
                            {}, class: "text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full",
                            data: { action: "plan-flow#syncAllocationRt" } %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <% end %>

      <%# Row 2: Amount (+ Mode sub-row) | Cadence (moved out of the old
          "More options" disclosure — round 26 R4 item 7d). %>
      <% if fm_kind %>
        <%# Row 2 (fun_money): Mode | Amount (left cell, C13 order 3+4) and
            Matching (right cell, order 5). Mode offers the four EXISTING
            values with the owner's labels (C3 = (a): no new enum value);
            the Amount input reuses the existing value control's contract
            (the mode-driven plan_allocation[value] vs [value_percent]
            rename is untouched — this is the form's only value control, so
            the plan-flow controller's mode handler finds it by name). %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-mode-group>
              <label class="block text-xs text-secondary" for="fm_mode_<%= node_id %>"><%= t(".mode_label") %></label>
              <select id="fm_mode_<%= node_id %>"
                      name="plan_allocation[mode]"
                      class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full"
                      data-action="change->plan-flow#syncAllocationMode">
                <option value="leftover" <%= "selected" if allocation.mode == "leftover" %>><%= t(".fm_mode_leftover") %></option>
                <option value="percent" <%= "selected" if allocation.mode == "percent" %>><%= t(".fm_mode_percent") %></option>
                <option value="specific" <%= "selected" if allocation.mode == "specific" %>><%= t(".fm_mode_specific") %></option>
                <option value="required" <%= "selected" if allocation.mode == "required" %>><%= t(".fm_mode_required") %></option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-field="value">
              <div data-allocation-field-state="editable">
                <label class="block text-xs text-secondary" for="fm_value_<%= node_id %>"
                       data-allocation-kind-label="value"
                       data-bill-label="<%= t('.value_label') %>"
                       data-savings-label="<%= t('.savings_value_label') %>"
                       data-fun-label="<%= t('.fun_value_label') %>"><%= amount_label %></label>
                <input type="text" id="fm_value_<%= node_id %>"
                       name="<%= allocation.mode == "percent" ? "plan_allocation[value_percent]" : "plan_allocation[value]" %>"
                       value="<%= allocation && %w[required specific].include?(allocation.mode) ? format("%.2f", allocation.value_cents.to_d / 100) : (allocation.mode == "percent" ? format("%.2f", allocation.value_percent.to_d * 100) : nil) %>"
                       placeholder="0.00"
                       <%= "disabled" if allocation.mode == "leftover" %>
                       class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full tabular-nums">
                <p class="text-xs text-secondary hidden"
                   data-allocation-required-hint
                   data-allocation-kind-hint="value"
                   data-bill-hint="<%= t('.required_hint') %>"
                   data-savings-hint="<%= t('.savings_value_hint') %>"
                   data-fun-hint="<%= t('.fun_value_hint') %>"><%= amount_hint %></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <%# Matching (C1): Equalize | Per Income — disabled when
                Ownership is Household (M2: per-user matching off; the field
                reads "— Household") and when the Distribution is
                "Individual Leftover by Allocations" (C10: it forces Per
                Income). %>
            <label class="block text-xs text-secondary" for="fm_matching_<%= node_id %>"><%= t(".matching_label") %></label>
            <select id="fm_matching_<%= node_id %>"
                    name="plan_allocation[matching]"
                    class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full"
                    <%= "disabled" if fm_ownership == "household" || fm_distribution == "individual_leftover" %>>
              <% if fm_ownership == "household" %>
                <option value="<%= fm_matching %>" selected><%= t(".matching_household") %></option>
              <% end %>
              <% if fm_distribution == "individual_leftover" && fm_ownership != "household" %>
                <option value="per_income" selected><%= t(".matching_per_income") %></option>
              <% end %>
              <option value="equalize" <%= "selected" if fm_ownership != "household" && fm_distribution != "individual_leftover" && fm_matching == "equalize" %>><%= t(".matching_equalize") %></option>
              <option value="per_income" <%= "selected" if fm_ownership != "household" && fm_distribution != "individual_leftover" && fm_matching == "per_income" %>><%= t(".matching_per_income") %></option>
            </select>
            <% if fm_rows_count > 1 %><p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".fun_money_multiple_hint") %></p><% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% else %>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <%# Amount: editable (mode-driven, the plan-flow controller renames
              it plan_allocation[value] vs [value_percent]) for a custom
              allocation; read-only monthly context for a linked bill.
              Round 26 R4 (item 8): the pencil rides INSIDE the value box. %>
          <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-field="value">
            <% if linked %>
              <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".amount_monthly_label") %></p>
              <div class="relative group">
                <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8 tabular-nums truncate">
                  <%= linked_monthly ? number_to_currency(linked_monthly / 100.0, currency: Current.family.currency) : "" %>
                </p>
                <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                  <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
                </span>
              </div>
              <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[value]" value="<%= format("%.2f", linked_monthly.to_d / 100) %>">
            <% else %>
              <div data-allocation-field-state="editable">
                <label class="block text-xs text-secondary"
                       for="plan_allocation_value"
                       data-allocation-kind-label="value"
                       data-bill-label="<%= t(".value_label") %>"
                       data-savings-label="<%= t(".savings_value_label") %>"
                       data-fun-label="<%= t(".fun_value_label") %>">
                  <%= amount_label %>
                </label>
                <%= form.text_field :value,
                                   value: allocation && %w[required specific].include?(allocation.mode) ? format("%.2f", allocation.value_cents.to_d / 100) : (allocation&.mode == "percent" ? format("%.2f", allocation.value_percent.to_d * 100) : nil),
                                   placeholder: "0.00",
                                   disabled: allocation.present? && allocation.mode == "leftover",
                                   class: "text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full tabular-nums",
                                   name: allocation&.mode == "percent" ? "plan_allocation[value_percent]" : "plan_allocation[value]",
                                   data: { action: nil } %>
                <p class="text-xs text-secondary" data-allocation-required-hint
                   data-allocation-kind-hint="value"
                   data-bill-hint="<%= t(".required_hint") %>"
                   data-savings-hint="<%= t(".savings_value_hint") %>"
                   data-fun-hint="<%= t(".fun_value_hint") %>">
                  <%= amount_hint %>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div data-allocation-field-state="locked" class="hidden">
                <div class="relative group">
                  <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8 tabular-nums truncate" data-allocation-locked-value></p>
                  <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                    <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
                  </span>
                </div>
                <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[value]" value="" disabled>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <%# Mode: valid for ALL FOUR kinds (round 25 R2: the Mode selector
              is visible + functional for Bill / Debt / Savings / Fun Money);
              a linked bill is always a required (monthly) figure, so the
              hidden input keeps the contract there (the group is hidden
              client-side for linked rows via #applyAllocationVisibility).
              The sub-row sits under the Amount (round 26 R4 item 7d). The
              group deliberately carries NO data-allocation-kinds attribute
              — the kind loop must never touch it. %>
          <% if linked %>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[mode]" value="required">
          <% else %>
            <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-mode-group>
              <%= form.label :mode, t(".mode_label"), class: "block text-xs text-secondary" %>
              <%= form.select :mode,
                              options_for_select(PlanAllocation.modes.values.map { |mode| [ t(".mode_#{mode}"), mode ] },
                                                 allocation&.mode || "required"),
                              {}, class: "text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full",
                              data: { action: "plan-flow#syncAllocationMode" } %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <%# Cadence: editable for a custom Bill / Debt allocation;
            read-only context for a linked bill; not applicable to a bucket
            kind (the gate hides it for savings / fun money).
            Round 26 R4 (item 8): the pencil rides INSIDE the value box. %>
        <div class="space-y-1" data-allocation-field="cadence">
          <% if linked %>
            <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".cadence_label") %></p>
            <div class="relative group">
              <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8">
                <%= allocation.cadence ? t(".cadence_#{allocation.cadence}") : "" %>
              </p>
              <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
              </span>
            </div>
            <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[cadence]" value="<%= allocation.cadence %>">
          <% else %>
            <div class="space-y-1<%= bucket_kind ? " hidden" : "" %>" data-allocation-field-state="editable" data-allocation-kinds="bill,debt">
              <%= form.label :cadence, t(".cadence_label"), class: "block text-xs text-secondary" %>
              <%= form.select :cadence,
                              options_for_select(PlanAllocation::CADENCES.map { |cadence| [ t(".cadence_#{cadence}"), cadence ] },
                                                 allocation&.cadence),
                              {}, class: "text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full" %>
            </div>
            <div data-allocation-field-state="locked" class="hidden">
              <div class="relative group">
                <p class="text-sm text-primary bg-surface-inset border border-subdued rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 pr-8" data-allocation-locked-value></p>
                <span data-allocation-pencil class="absolute top-2 right-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100">
                  <%= render DS::Tooltip.new(icon: "pencil", text: t(".locked_tooltip"), as: :span) %>
                </span>
              </div>
              <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[cadence]" value="" disabled>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Row 3: Bank source — the labeled row (round 26 R4 item 6): the
          trigger shows ONLY the active selection (avatar + name +
          ****last4, or the profile icon + "None Selected"); clicking
          opens the floating dropdown panel rendered after the form.
          The kind hint below is the data-allocation-kind-hint the
          relabel loop rewrites per kind. %>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-inset p-2">
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->plan-flow#toggleBankSource"
                data-allocation-bank-trigger
                data-allocation-bank-none="<%= t('.none_selected') %>"
                class="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-2 min-h-11 rounded-xl px-1 cursor-pointer">
          <span class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
            <span class="text-xs text-secondary shrink-0"><%= t(".section_bank_source") %></span>
            <% bank_account = allocation&.account %>
            <% if bank_account %>
              <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center relative"
                    data-allocation-bank-chip>
                <span class="text-sm font-medium text-secondary"><%= (bank_account.name.to_s.strip.first || "?").upcase %></span>
                <% if bank_account.plan_flow_avatar_url.present? %>
                  <img src="<%= bank_account.plan_flow_avatar_url %>" alt="" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" onerror="this.remove()">
                <% end %>
              </span>
              <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center text-secondary hidden"
                    data-allocation-bank-none-icon>
                <%= icon "user", size: "sm" %>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm text-primary truncate" data-allocation-bank-name><%= bank_account.name %></span>
              <% if (bank_last4 = @account_last4s[bank_account.id]) %>
                <span class="text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums" data-allocation-bank-last4>****<%= bank_last4 %></span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums hidden" data-allocation-bank-last4></span>
              <% end %>
            <% else %>
              <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center relative hidden"
                    data-allocation-bank-chip>?</span>
              <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center text-secondary"
                    data-allocation-bank-none-icon>
                <%= icon "user", size: "sm" %>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm text-secondary truncate" data-allocation-bank-name><%= t(".none_selected") %></span>
              <span class="text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums hidden" data-allocation-bank-last4></span>
            <% end %>
          </span>
          <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0" %>
        </button>
        <p class="text-xs text-secondary" data-allocation-kind-hint="account"
           data-bill-hint="<%= t(".source_bank_hint") %>"
           data-savings-hint="<%= t(".savings_account_hint") %>"
           data-fun-hint="<%= t(".fun_account_hint") %>">
          <%= account_hint %>
        </p>
      </div>

      <%# Row 4: Category — the trigger IS the labeled row (round 26 R4
          item 7b: the colored icon chip mirrors the popup rows; the old
          disclosure wrapper is gone). The radio list + the floating panel
          are the DS::Popover verbatim (same change action, same max-h-64
          scroll window, fixed z-50 — the radios stay in the form, so the
          save contract (plan_allocation[category_id]) is unchanged). The
          row chips carry data-allocation-cat-row-chip so
          #allocationCategorySummary can clone the checked row's chip into
          the trigger (the no-category row carries a neutral ? chip with
          the same marker). %>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-inset p-2">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <%= render DS::Popover.new(variant: "button", no_padding: true, placement: "bottom-end", max_width: "24rem") do |popover| %>
            <% popover.with_button(class: "w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-between gap-2 cursor-pointer min-h-11") do %>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
                <span class="text-xs text-secondary shrink-0"><%= t(".category_label") %></span>
                <% if category_selection %>
                  <% if category_selection.lucide_icon.present? %>
                    <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"
                          style="background-color: color-mix(in oklab, <%= category_selection.color %> 10%, transparent); color: <%= category_selection.color %>;"
                          data-allocation-category-icon-chip>
                      <%= icon(category_selection.lucide_icon, size: "sm", color: "current") %>
                    </span>
                  <% else %>
                    <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium"
                          style="background-color: color-mix(in oklab, <%= category_selection.color %> 10%, transparent); color: <%= category_selection.color %>;"
                          data-allocation-category-icon-chip>
                      <%= category_selection.display_name.to_s[0].to_s.upcase %>
                    </span>
                  <% end %>
                <% else %>
                  <%# Round 31A (C7, §4.1): the category-less fun_money row's
                      band renders with the app's income green (the sankey
                      kind fallback, #10A861) — the trigger chip matches it;
                      the neutral "?" chip stays for every other kind. %>
                  <% if fm_kind %>
                    <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium"
                          style="background-color: color-mix(in oklab, #10A861 10%, transparent); color: #10A861;"
                          data-allocation-category-icon-chip>?</span>
                  <% else %>
                    <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium text-secondary bg-subdued"
                          data-allocation-category-icon-chip>?</span>
                  <% end %>
                <% end %>
                <span class="text-sm text-primary truncate" data-allocation-category-selection><%= category_selection_text %></span>
              </span>
              <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0 planflow-cat-chevron transition-transform" %>
            <% end %>
            <% popover.with_custom_content do %>
              <div class="p-1 space-y-1">
                <div class="max-h-64 overflow-y-auto rounded-lg border border-subdued bg-container p-1.5"
                     data-action="change->plan-flow#syncAllocationCategory">
                <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
                  <input type="radio" name="plan_allocation[category_id]" value="" class="sr-only"
                         data-allocation-category-name="<%= t(".category_none") %>"
                         <%= "checked" if category_id.nil? %>>
                  <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium text-secondary bg-subdued"
                        data-allocation-cat-row-chip>?</span>
                  <span class="text-sm text-secondary"><%= t(".category_none") %></span>
                </label>
                <% categories_list.each do |category| %>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
                    <input type="radio" name="plan_allocation[category_id]" value="<%= category.id %>" class="sr-only"
                           data-allocation-category-name="<%= category.display_name %>"
                           <%= "checked" if category_id.present? && category_id.to_s == category.id.to_s %>>
                    <% if category.lucide_icon.present? %>
                      <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"
                            style="background-color: color-mix(in oklab, <%= category.color %> 10%, transparent); color: <%= category.color %>;"
                            data-allocation-cat-row-chip>
                        <%= icon(category.lucide_icon, size: "sm", color: "current") %>
                      </span>
                    <% else %>
                      <span class="h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium"
                            style="background-color: color-mix(in oklab, <%= category.color %> 10%, transparent); color: <%= category.color %>;"
                            data-allocation-cat-row-chip>
                        <%= category.display_name.to_s[0].to_s.upcase %>
                      </span>
                    <% end %>
                    <span class="text-sm text-primary truncate <%= "pl-3" if category.subcategory? %>"><%= category.display_name %></span>
                  </label>
                <% end %>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-secondary px-1"><%= t(".category_hint") %></p>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 pt-1 border-t border-subdued">
        <% if is_new %>
          <span></span>
        <% else %>
          <%# The delete form is a sibling (below), not a nested form —
              HTML forbids nested <form>, and the browser would hoist the
              Delete button into this form. The form= attribute points the
              button at its own form. In-place delete (owner round 3, R1):
              the sibling form's in-place submit handler fetches the
              destroy and the node shrinks out — no reload. %>
          <button type="submit"
                  form="allocation_delete_<%= allocation.id %>"
                  class="text-sm text-destructive hover:underline">
            <%= t(".delete") %>
          </button>
        <% end %>
        <%# In-place save (owner round 3, R1/R7): see the form's data-action. %>
        <button type="submit"
                class="text-sm bg-primary text-on-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 hover:opacity-90">
          <%= t(".save") %>
        </button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <%# Round 26 R4 (item 6): the BANK SOURCE floating dropdown panel —
        OUTSIDE the form (a same-name radio group + the form's hidden
        plan_allocation[account_id] input in one <form> would serialize as
        an array), but still a DOM descendant of the dialog's content
        target, so a click inside it never looks like a backdrop click
        (round 26 R3 clickOutside lesson — the panel rendered OUTSIDE the
        content target is what closed the dialog on every panel click).
        Hidden by default; plan_flow_controller positions it under the
        trigger on open (position:fixed z-50, viewport-clamped — a
        position:fixed descendant of the top-layer <dialog> is NOT clipped
        by the inner overflow-auto, the same pattern the category popover
        panel uses in this same dialog). The fragment root keeps
        data-flow-chrome="allocation-bank-rows" (the in-place swap target);
        its max-h-64 overflow-y-auto is the panel's scroll window. %>
    <div data-allocation-bank-panel class="hidden fixed z-50 w-72">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-subdued bg-container p-1.5"
           data-action="change->plan-flow#syncBankSource">
        <%= render "plan_flows/allocation_bank_rows",
              bank_rows: bank_rows, checked_account_id: allocation&.account_id,
              account_last4s: @account_last4s %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%# Round 31A (C2): the Distribution floating radio panel — same
        pattern as the Split Behavior panel in the bank config dialog: OUTSIDE
        the form (a same-name radio group + the form's hidden
        plan_allocation[distribution] input in one <form> would serialize as
        an array), a DOM descendant of the dialog's content target (backdrop-
        click lesson), hidden by default; plan_flow_controller#toggleFun
        Distribution positions it under the trigger on open (position:fixed
        z-50, viewport-clamped). "Percentage of Pooled" reveals the
        per-member percent inputs (C9) below the radio list. %>
    <div data-allocation-fm-distribution-panel class="hidden fixed z-50 w-72">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-subdued bg-container p-1.5 space-y-1"
           data-action="change->plan-flow#syncFunDistribution">
        <% PlanAllocation::FM_DISTRIBUTIONS.each do |distribution| %>
          <label class="flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1.5 cursor-pointer rounded-md hover:bg-surface-inset">
            <input type="radio" name="fun_distribution" value="<%= distribution %>" class="sr-only"
                   data-fm-distribution-radio="<%= distribution %>"
                   <%= "checked" if fm_distribution == distribution %>>
            <span class="text-sm <%= fm_distribution == distribution ? "text-primary" : "text-secondary" %>"><%= t(".distribution_#{distribution}") %></span>
          </label>
        <% end %>
        <div data-allocation-fm-percent-inputs class="<%= fm_distribution == "percent" ? "" : "hidden" %> space-y-1 px-1 pt-1">
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".distribution_percent_hint") %></p>
          <% fm_members.each do |member| %>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm text-secondary truncate"><%= member.display_name %></span>
              <input type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.01"
                     name="fun_distribution_percent"
                     data-fm-percent-member="<%= member.id %>"
                     value="<%= fm_percents[member.id.to_s] %>"
                     placeholder="0.00"
                     class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1 bg-container text-primary w-24 tabular-nums"
                     data-action="change->plan-flow#syncFunPercent">
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <% unless is_new %>
      <%= form_with url: flow_allocation_destroy_plan_path(allocation.id),
                    method: :delete,
                    id: "allocation_delete_#{allocation.id}",
                    class: "sr-only",
                    data: { turbo: "false", plan_flow_inplace: "true" } do %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :scenario, @scenario.id if @scenario %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
